<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Entitlements for the APPEX ONLY - Carabiner.app itself must never be
	  sandboxed (it shells out to yt-dlp/ffmpeg and writes ~/Downloads), and a
	  process is governed by its own signature, so sandboxing the appex does not
	  leak into the app (the same isolation gotcha #20 rests on, from the other
	  direction).

	  app-sandbox is not optional politeness: pkd refuses to register an
	  unsandboxed plug-in at discovery, logging "Ignoring mis-configured plugin
	  ... plug-ins must be sandboxed" - measured 2026-08-16, and the reason the
	  extension never appeared in Safari's Extensions list. The failure is
	  silent from Safari's side, which is exactly the shape the manual
	  checklist's item 1 feared; the fear was just aimed at the wrong bundle.

	  network.client matches Apple's own web-extension template. The extension's
	  fetch to 127.0.0.1:51847 runs in Safari's extension processes rather than
	  this appex, but the native side is sandboxed with it and the entitlement
	  is what the template grants - dropping it is an experiment to run on
	  purpose someday, not a cleanup.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
